    description: "The Bed 5 Wisteria forms a permanent woody framework along the boundary, carrying hanging lilac racemes in May before vigorous leafy shoots extend through summer. Left alone, those whippy stems can travel metres, shade the bed and reach weak structures; disciplined training converts that energy into short flowering spurs. The species is not recorded, so the profile does not pretend that flower direction or stem twining has proved Chinese or Japanese wisteria.",
