    problem: { name: "Death after flowering", sign: "One central rosette browns after its flower stalk fades", response: "This is normal monocarpic growth: remove that rosette and guide surrounding offsets into the space." },
    about: "Sempervivum are mountain succulents from Europe and Asia, adapted to exposed rock through water-storing leaves and clonal offsets. Seasonal colour is fluid, so identifying cultivars from a summer photograph is unreliable. The colony is maintained by its younger offsets rather than by keeping every parent rosette alive indefinitely.", provenance: "Genus is secure; the Stone Bed is treated as a mixed houseleek collection without invented cultivar names.", family: "Crassulaceae", genus: "Sempervivum", foliage: "Evergreen and succulent", habit: "Rosette-forming with stoloniferous offsets", role: "Low living mosaic through the gravel", observation: "Multiple rosettes fill dry gaps and maintain colour through winter.", status: "Photograph individual rosettes seasonally before attempting any cultivar identification.", source: RHS.sempervivum,
