    description: "The Stonecrop threads fleshy, water-storing stems through the gravel and over nearby stones, creating a low mat before its small starry flowers appear in summer or autumn. It tolerates heat and dry soil that would stop most border perennials, but growth becomes soft and sparse in shade or rich compost. ‘Trailing Sedum’ covers several possible species, so leaf arrangement and a clear flower photograph are still needed for a sound identity.",
